            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0290" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v04/pg264"/>

                <head>132. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and
                    the Assistant Secretary of State for Far Eastern Affairs (Hilsman)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d132-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1963-09-19T10:23:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September 19, 1963—10:23
                        a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">TELEPHONE CALL TO MR HILSMAN</p>
                <p>Sec referred to telegram about Maneli<anchor n="2" xml:id="d132-f2"/>—he wonders
                    if it is not better since there are one or two utterly simple and fundamental
                    things that are crucial at most to find out from the British Amb whether this
                    means something on the spot de facto partition or call the whole thing off. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] Sec worried about signal that would go to the
                    North until we go to Maneli in this situation and say what about a cease-fire.
                    It seems to him we can find out what the answer is to the central question
                    without exposing ourselves. Sec asked H to give it some thought.</p>
                <pb facs="0291" n="265" xml:id="pg265"/>
                <p>H just reading 544<anchor n="3" xml:id="d132-f3"/> and he seems to want some of
                    our thinking re para 5 he asks for it-Sec said they have not figured anything
                    out there and his guess is to wait until the trip occurs and see what happens
                    there. Can’t see action here. H then said it is just that para 5 asked for our
                    thinking which we could get out. Sec said o.k.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
